The default firmware evaluation graph uses the Rete integration fork from
https://github.com/evelant/rete at revision
2d0781838aa03370b739d4003bcd1bdd5bbb0c6c on branch
codex/link-data-receipts. That revision descends from
90570cafc812b3025011cb690ec74a27f287cb3f, based on upstream
https://github.com/s-retlaw/rete revision
9bcb7d3e482b7df100622f2a0d9e53ba3bb7a743. The fork retains upstream's
MIT OR Apache-2.0 declaration in its package metadata and README. Fork tag
firmware-pin-90570ca names the predecessor; the current exact revision has no
designated durable tag.

The checked LXMF compatibility corpus is generated from Python LXMF 1.0.1 at
revision fab12ad9bf9f997797034950f289fe41a79dcf5a and Python RNS at revision
50e03a24e8e10256363f6b73af7f6804ddb90e6f. Their exact Reticulum License
notices are retained in LICENSE-RETICULUM for LXMF and
LICENSE-RETICULUM-RNS for RNS. Those sources are protocol authorities and test
peers; they are not linked into the firmware. Project-owned
`reticulum-lxmf-wire` source is independently implemented from the documented
wire behavior and remains under the project's MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms.

The separate Leviculum comparison package is AGPL-3.0-or-later. See
docs/provenance.md and Cargo.lock for the exact source and dependency graph.
